00:05:57,391 --> 00:06:03,391
Child. Captive. Killer.

2
00:11:54,782 --> 00:12:00,782
Beasts of No Nation is a drama, war film directed by Cary Joji Fukunaga.

3
00:17:52,173 --> 00:17:58,173
Based on the experiences of Agu, a child fighting in
the civil war of a West African country.

4
00:23:49,565 --> 00:23:55,565
Follows Agu's journey as he's forced to join a group of soldiers.

5
00:29:46,956 --> 00:29:52,956
While he fears his commander and many of the men around him, his fledgling childhood has been brutally shattered by the
war raging through his country, and he is at first torn between conflicting revulsion and fascination.

6
00:35:44,347 --> 00:35:50,347
Agu, played by Abraham Attah.

7
00:41:41,739 --> 00:41:47,739
Commandant, played by Idris Elba.

8
00:47:39,130 --> 00:47:45,130
Strika, played by Emmanuel Nii Adom Quaye.

9
00:53:36,521 --> 00:53:42,521
Sergeant Gaz, played by Opeyemi Fagbohungbe.

10
00:59:33,913 --> 00:59:39,913
Dike, played by Emmanuel Affadzi.

11
01:05:31,304 --> 01:05:37,304
Father Friday, played by Richard Pepple.

12
01:11:28,695 --> 01:11:34,695
Beasts of No Nation is a 2015 American war drama film written,
co-produced, shot, and directed by Cary Joji Fukunaga.

13
01:17:26,086 --> 01:17:32,086
It follows a young boy who becomes a child soldier as his
country experiences a horrific civil war.

14
01:23:23,478 --> 01:23:29,478
Shot in Ghana and starring Idris Elba, Abraham Attah, Ama K.

15
01:29:20,869 --> 01:29:26,869
Abebrese, Grace Nortey, David Dontoh, and Opeyemi Fagbohungbe, the film is based on the 2005 novel of
the same name by Uzodinma Iweala, the book itself being named after a Fela Kuti album.

16
01:35:18,260 --> 01:35:24,260
It was screened in the main competition section of the 72nd Venice International
Film Festival, where Attah won the Marcello Mastroianni Award.

17
01:41:15,652 --> 01:41:21,652
The film was shown in the Special Presentation section of the 2015 Toronto International Film Festival, and
released on Netflix globally and in a limited release by Bleecker Street on October 16, 2015.

18
01:47:13,043 --> 01:47:19,043
It is the first film to be released directly on Netflix.

19
01:53:10,434 --> 01:53:16,434
The film received positive reviews from critics and numerous accolades.

20
01:59:07,826 --> 01:59:13,826
Elba's performance earned nominations for the BAFTA, Golden Globe, Spirit, and
SAG Award for Best Supporting Actor, winning the latter two.

21
02:05:05,217 --> 02:05:11,217
The film explores themes of guerrilla warfare, civil war,
based on novel or book, africa, refugee.

22
02:11:02,608 --> 02:11:08,608
The tone is dark and emotional.
